On Oct 21, 6:31 pm, Dragontamer <prtig...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Third, is there any chance that items in a BoH can get burnt from
> a fire trap? I know that water can wipe out scrolls / potions (learned
> it unfortunately... the hard way) so can fire do the same thing?

Items in a Bag are safe from fire/cold damage. Noncursed Oilskin sacks
also prevent water damage, so things inside those are pretty much safe
from anything.

> Finally, I keep a habit of having emergency scrolls and potions open
> in my inventory (teleport and extra/full healing). They tend to burn/
> boil
> when I get hit by a trap. So are there any random tips to either
> prevent
> fire traps from effecting them, or how to stop fire traps in general?

You could try some alternatives. Use wands of teleport instead of
scrolls. Blessed Tins of Nurse meat are a possible alternative to
potions of healing, they're won't boil/freeze like potions, and will
fully heal you when you eat them. However, it will take two turns to
consume (one to open, one to eat), and will make you a cannibal if
you're human, so they're not quite perfect subsitutes.



